2026-09-27T04:47:41.0866498Z Update Note
2026-09-27T04:47:41.0866801Z ===========
2026-09-27T04:47:41.0867175Z Please use this repository instead of ppa:fkrull/deadsnakes.
2026-09-27T04:47:41.0867420Z 
2026-09-27T04:47:41.0867688Z Reporting Issues
2026-09-27T04:47:41.0867891Z ================
2026-09-27T04:47:41.0868075Z 
2026-09-27T04:47:41.0868234Z Issues can be reported in the master issue tracker at:
2026-09-27T04:47:41.0868562Z https://github.com/deadsnakes/issues/issues
2026-09-27T04:47:41.0868736Z 
2026-09-27T04:47:41.0868848Z Supported Ubuntu and Python Versions
2026-09-27T04:47:41.0869161Z ====================================
2026-09-27T04:47:41.0869291Z 
2026-09-27T04:47:41.0869657Z - Ubuntu 22.04 (jammy) Python3.7+ (NOT Python3.10)
2026-09-27T04:47:41.0870041Z - Ubuntu 24.04 (noble) Python3.7+ (NOT Python3.12)
2026-09-27T04:47:41.0870351Z - Ubuntu 26.04 (resolute) Python3.7+ (NOT Python3.14)
2026-09-27T04:47:41.0870829Z - Note: Python 3.10 (jammy), Python3.12 (noble), Python3.14 (resolute) are not provided by deadsnakes as upstream ubuntu provides those packages.
2026-09-27T04:47:41.0871223Z 
2026-09-27T04:47:41.0871319Z Why some packages aren't built:
2026-09-27T04:47:41.0871708Z - Note: for 22.04+, older python versions requre libssl<3 so they are not currently built
2026-09-27T04:47:41.0872154Z - If you need these, reach out to asottile to set up a private ppa
2026-09-27T04:47:41.0872363Z 
2026-09-27T04:47:41.0872603Z The packages may also work on other versions of Ubuntu or Debian, but that is not tested or supported.
2026-09-27T04:47:41.0872871Z 
2026-09-27T04:47:41.0872980Z Packages
2026-09-27T04:47:41.0873201Z ========
2026-09-27T04:47:41.0873325Z 
2026-09-27T04:47:41.0874123Z The packages provided here are loosely based on the debian upstream packages with some modifications to make them more usable as non-default pythons and on ubuntu.  As such, the packages follow debian's patterns and often do not include a full python distribution with just `apt install python#.#`.  Here is a list of packages that may be useful along with the default install:
2026-09-27T04:47:41.0874959Z 
2026-09-27T04:47:41.0875135Z - `python#.#-dev`: includes development headers for building C extensions
2026-09-27T04:47:41.0875563Z - `python#.#-venv`: provides the standard library `venv` module
2026-09-27T04:47:41.0875933Z - `python#.#-distutils`: provides the standard library `distutils` module
2026-09-27T04:47:41.0876375Z - `python#.#-lib2to3`: provides the `2to3-#.#` utility as well as the standard library `lib2to3` module
2026-09-27T04:47:41.0876784Z - `python#.#-gdbm`: provides the standard library `dbm.gnu` module
2026-09-27T04:47:41.0877132Z - `python#.#-tk`: provides the standard library `tkinter` module
2026-09-27T04:47:41.0877361Z 
2026-09-27T04:47:41.0877725Z Third-Party Python Modules
2026-09-27T04:47:41.0877956Z ==========================
2026-09-27T04:47:41.0878126Z 
2026-09-27T04:47:41.0878801Z Python modules in the official Ubuntu repositories are packaged to work with the Python interpreters from the official repositories. Accordingly, they generally won't work with the Python interpreters from this PPA. As an exception, pure-Python modules for Python 3 will work, but any compiled extension modules won't.
2026-09-27T04:47:41.0879837Z 
2026-09-27T04:47:41.0880284Z To install 3rd-party Python modules, you should use the common Python packaging tools.  For an introduction into the Python packaging ecosystem and its tools, refer to the Python Packaging User Guide:
2026-09-27T04:47:41.0880928Z https://packaging.python.org/installing/
2026-09-27T04:47:41.0881114Z 
